  "substituteBlankTrap": "BCD 16 / octal 20 (A bit only) is the substitute blank ƀ, a distinct 1410 graphic named in A22-0526-3 Figure 4 'Symbol Names' p.7 — SCNLA assembles as D (A)(B) ƀ while SCNLS assembles as D (A)(B) blank (true blank, octal 00). Emitting an ASCII space for SCNLA turns it into SCNLS, a different instruction. The same character is BNT1/BNT2's d in §6.2."
